From: XR1710G AP project
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: context-scope explicit TC bridge templates and revoke on topology changes

MAC-only FDB fallback is removed. Cache hits require namespace cookie, ingress
ifindex, bridge ifindex, actual VLAN/protocol and exact MACs from an explicitly
declared TC redirect rule. Reject wildcard/unknown-domain templates. Invalidate
L2 subflows and quarantine cached templates on netdevice topology events; owner
must destroy/recreate the TC rule to authorize it again. Hardware FOE ABI is
unchanged. NPU/PPE boot policies remain off. No automatic VLAN bypass, no claim
of measured acceleration or complete netfilter authorization of bridge traffic.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
